00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.829 align:start position:0%
an individual weather event is not  the same thing as climate a single  stronger than usual unseasonably late  hurricane  doesn't really tell us anything about  what's happening with the climate but  multiple decades of higher high  temperatures  lower low temperatures unseasonably warm  unseasonably cold  stronger and more and stronger  hurricanes during hurricane season all  of those things not just one day  start to tell us about the climate of a  place and whether the climate is  changing
 

